      "body": "## Claude Code Review\n\nThis pull request is from a fork — automated review is disabled. A repository maintainer can comment `@claude review` to run a one-time review.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47013#pullrequestreview-4645021155",
      "id": 4645021155,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-07-07T12:22:23Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "claude[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Checked this against the pattern #46908 established for the same problem (`get_attention_context()` / `mla_attention.py`) — the `if isinstance(slot_mapping, list): slot_mapping = slot_mapping[0]` fix here matches that precedent exactly, including the \"[0] is the base model\" comment convention and the test structure (constructing a `ForwardContext` with `slot_mapping=[{...}]` and asserting the unwrapped dict is what reaches `do_kv_cache_update`).\n\nAlso went looking for any other `forward_context.slot_mapping` consumer this PR (and #46908/#46830 before it) might have missed. There are 8 references repo-wide; the only one not covered by either PR is `whisper_causal.py`, but that one's deliberately not affected — it explicitly builds its own transformed `slot_mapping` off `attn_metadata` instead and has a comment saying exactly why it avoids `forward_context.slot_mapping`. So this PR's two additions (`extract_hidden_states.py`, `deepseek_v32/nvidia/attention.py`) look like the complete remaining set, not a partial fix.\n",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47013#pullrequestreview-4670738820",
      "id": 4670738820,
      "state": "APPROVED",
